WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:03.230
- You've said that this album
is your most honest album

00:00:03.230 --> 00:00:04.600
so why do you think so?

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:07.140
- Because I started so young,

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:09.520
there's a huge part of me
that didn't get a chance

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:13.120
to develop my identity
in a normal setting,

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:15.580
so when I was working with Disney,

00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:18.780
it was the best time of my
life and I had a great time.

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:20.230
I have nothing but good things to say,

00:00:20.230 --> 00:00:23.250
but it was a bit more controlled.

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:26.203
There were certain things
that I was, you know,

00:00:27.910 --> 00:00:31.590
had to do and not maybe go into,

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:33.580
like figuring out what my sound would be.

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:36.840
So, I've constantly been trying to make

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:38.260
my music better and better.

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:42.210
Because, I know that people may not think

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:43.330
I'm the greatest singer,

00:00:43.330 --> 00:00:48.320
but I just work my ass off and
I love, I really love writing

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:51.200
and creating and creating
melodies and growing

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:55.280
and I felt like this was my
chance to say all the things

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:57.580
that I wanted to say in that way,

00:00:57.580 --> 00:00:59.670
which was talking about relationships

00:00:59.670 --> 00:01:02.050
and talking about difficult times

00:01:02.050 --> 00:01:07.050
or being vulnerable or
being stuck in your head,

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:09.500
'cause, you know, I can do that a lot,

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:11.090
but I wanted it to feel good.

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:14.010
I wanted it to feel
like every word mattered

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:16.243
and you could feel it physically.

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:18.990
I'm still in the studio actually now

00:01:18.990 --> 00:01:21.970
because I feel like it's inspired me

00:01:21.970 --> 00:01:22.970
and I just wanna keep going.

00:01:22.970 --> 00:01:24.030
- It's a creative time, yeah.

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:24.863
Isn't that funny?

00:01:24.863 --> 00:01:25.960
You make an, that always
happens to me too.

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:28.340
I make and album and then
after I'm releasing it

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:29.840
right while I'm doing it,
I'm doing another one.

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:30.737
- Exactly.
- It always happens like that.

00:01:30.737 --> 00:01:32.020
- I'm like, I don't I don't, just

00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:33.160
- But I wanna point something out

00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:36.620
because doing "The Voice" especially

00:01:36.620 --> 00:01:37.660
has been really interesting

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:39.000
because a lot of people always think,

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:40.187
'cause you said, Oh I
know people may not say

00:01:40.187 --> 00:01:41.350
I'm the best singer.

00:01:41.350 --> 00:01:43.240
The best singer in the world,

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:44.820
talking to everyone in
the world right now,

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:47.990
is not the loudest and is not the,

00:01:47.990 --> 00:01:49.420
oh my god you have to
sing like Whitney Houston

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:50.253
every time you do it.

00:01:50.253 --> 00:01:52.910
The best singers in the world move you.

00:01:52.910 --> 00:01:56.100
And that comes from all
different sounds and styles,

00:01:56.100 --> 00:02:00.020
so from a singer to a singer,
it's beautiful what you do

00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:02.670
and I love your record
and I love big huge songs,

00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:04.670
but I love singing your music.

00:02:04.670 --> 00:02:06.260
It means something and it moves people,

00:02:06.260 --> 00:02:09.828
so don't ever negate your
gift, 'cause it's powerful.

00:02:09.828 --> 00:02:10.856
(audience cheers)

00:02:10.856 --> 00:02:12.306
That's what what I wanna say.

